@startuml AD_User_Registration_Workflow
!theme cerulean-outline
title User Registration Workflow
footer AdventureWorks Sales BI Platform

|#e8f0fe|User (Browser)|
|#e8f4e8|React Frontend|
|#fff3e0|ASP.NET Core Backend|
|#fce4ec|Identity / Database|

|User (Browser)|
start
:Open Register page;

:Enter **username**, **email**,\nand **password**;

|React Frontend|
#LightYellow:Validate input fields;

note right
  All four password rules are
  evaluated in parallel on submit.
  Any single failure blocks the
  POST request from being sent.
end note

fork
  if (Password length >= 6?) then (no)
    #LightCoral:Show error:\n"Password must be at least\n6 characters";
    detach
  else (yes)
  endif
fork again
  if (Password contains digit?) then (no)
    #LightCoral:Show error:\n"Password requires a digit";
    detach
  else (yes)
  endif
fork again
  if (Password contains uppercase?) then (no)
    #LightCoral:Show error:\n"Password requires\nan uppercase letter";
    detach
  else (yes)
  endif
fork again
  if (Password contains lowercase?) then (no)
    #LightCoral:Show error:\n"Password requires\na lowercase letter";
    detach
  else (yes)
  endif
end fork

#LightGreen:All frontend validations pass;

#LightBlue:POST /api/auth/register\n{ username, email, password }\n(RegisterDto);

|ASP.NET Core Backend|
:AuthController.Register()\nreceives RegisterDto;

:Create AppUser\n{ UserName, Email,\n  EmailConfirmed = true };

|Identity / Database|
#LightBlue:UserManager.CreateAsync(user, password);

if (Email already exists\nor Identity rules fail?) then (yes)
  :Return IdentityResult.Errors;
  |ASP.NET Core Backend|
  #LightCoral:Return **400 BadRequest**\nwith error descriptions;
  |React Frontend|
  #LightCoral:Display server errors\n(e.g. "Duplicate email");
  detach
else (no)
  #LightGreen:User created successfully;
endif

|ASP.NET Core Backend|
:AddToRoleAsync(user, **"User"**);

note right
  JwtTokenService signs the token
  with the HMAC key from config.
  Claims embedded: uid
  (NameIdentifier), username,
  email, and roles[].
end note

#LightBlue:JwtTokenService.CreateTokenAsync(user)\ngenerates JWT with claims\n(uid, username, email, roles);

#LightGreen:Return **200 OK**\nAuthResponseDto {\n  Token, ExpiresAtUtc,\n  Username, Email, Roles };

|React Frontend|
:Receive AuthResponseDto;

:Store **token** in localStorage\nStore user info (username,\nemail, roles);

#LightGreen:Redirect to **Home** page;

|User (Browser)|
:User sees Home page\nas authenticated user;

stop

caption Registration — POST /api/auth/register — ASP.NET Identity validation + JWT issuance
@enduml
